From 7d6cf7a718fb2f00f095410daa0033352933f9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:02:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] Plugins: character values with when the game reported
 them; shops per character

The character event now says when the game last reported each value
(`seenAt`: Odyle energy, each content count, shop limit and craft, Kinah
by the game's own time, Abyss Points), also when it reported one
unchanged. A plugin keeping values per character (Roster) took the first
time it saw a value: the same count reported again a week later looked a
week old, and past the reset it showed 0.

Shop limits and crafts, which the game sends only as the shop or the
crafting window opens, were dropped at every login. They are now kept by
character and come back when that character plays again.

A login's Kinah that comes after the self record naming who logged in
(the list, the record, then `a5 ff`) is theirs at once; it waited for the
next self record, minutes later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RahWACwaxzLAcYgwc9jk8C
